From: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
Subject: ASoC: qcom: q6afe-rtproxy-pcm: voice call audio as a sound card

New q6afe child component "qcom,q6afe-rtproxy-pcm" providing PCMs for
voice call audio (capture = call downlink on AFE RT proxy port 0x2000,
playback = call uplink on 0x2001, S16_LE mono, 8/16 kHz, 20 ms frames)
and a minimal machine driver "qcom,q6afe-rtproxy-card" (dummy codec).

The card has two links: "CS Voice" (pcm device 0, DAI "q6afe-rtproxy")
for circuit switched calls and "VoLTE Voice" (pcm device 1, DAI
"q6afe-rtproxy-volte") for the Q6VOICE_PATH_VOLTE session. Both use the
same AFE RT proxy ports and vocproc topology, so CS and VoLTE are
mutually exclusive: opening a stream of one while a stream of the other
is open fails with -EBUSY.

The commands are paced by an hrtimer, one READ_V2/WRITE_V2 per frame (the
DSP sends no RT proxy events and returns silence for burst reads). The
first prepared stream maps the shared buffer, starts and registers both
proxy ports and starts the q6voice path (q6voice_start_path with the proxy
ports, MVM attach, START_VOICE); the last hw_free/close, or removal of the
q6afe parent, tears everything down. A stream without DSP response for 1 s
is stopped with an xrun.

Three opt-in debug module parameters are read when the voice path starts
(so a change in /sys/module/q6afe_rtproxy_pcm/parameters/ applies to the
next open):

 trace       log every q6voice APR command (service, opcode, session
             handle, rc, DSP status) while the path is started
 attach      default|mvm|cvs|both, overrides cfg.attach
 start_voice -1 (default), 0 or 1, overrides cfg.start_voice

The effective path configuration is logged on every path start.

Built on the q6afe RT proxy API and the q6voice path selection.

Signed-off-by: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
